# Hash-pinned data (selection locks, SHA256SUMS, frozen fixtures, per-file
# provenance): every checkout must yield the EXACT bytes the pins were
# computed from. Windows autocrlf converted the LF text sources to CRLF on
# checkout, silently breaking frozen-fixture reproducibility (audit
# 2026-09-18: data/pilot-v2/sources/HumanEval-LICENSE.txt failed its pinned
# sha256 locally while CI -- a fresh LF checkout -- passed).
data/** -text

# Frozen manifests pin the sha256 of these builders' ON-DISK bytes
# (``digest(Path(__file__).read_bytes())`` -- line-ending dependent). The
# pins were computed from LF files (Linux CI); a Windows autocrlf checkout
# hands the builders CRLF copies, their self-hash no longer matches the
# frozen manifest, and byte-reproducibility fails locally while CI passes
# (audit 2026-09-18: data/pilot-v2/manifest.json builder_sha256=fada6301 is
# the LF form of scripts/prepare_coding_pilot.py; data/specialist-v1 pins
# the same file as audited_parser_sha256 and prepare_specialist_data.py as
# builder_sha256). Force LF working-tree bytes for exactly these scripts.
scripts/prepare_coding_pilot.py text eol=lf
scripts/prepare_specialist_data.py text eol=lf

# Receipt-pinned pilot artifacts (capability-build receipts pin the raw
# sha256 of these files' on-disk bytes): same failure class as data/**.
# The 09-18 receipt pins judgment-teacher.json / judgment-student-*.json
# over CRLF bytes, so the LF-normalised index copy fails its pin on any
# fresh checkout; the 09-19 receipt pins the deepapply-run artifacts over
# LF bytes, which a Windows autocrlf checkout would have converted. No
# conversion anywhere: the index keeps whatever bytes the pins were
# computed from, so every checkout on every platform yields them exactly
# (pre-commit pin audit 2026-09-19; the judgment files are re-committed
# in their pinned CRLF form).
experiments/glm53_flash_pilot/** -text